# =============================================================================
# What `gcloud run deploy --source .` uploads to Cloud Build.
# =============================================================================
# This is a *different* list from `.dockerignore`, and the difference matters.
#
# `.dockerignore` trims the context Docker sees once the build has started, so
# it can exclude the Dockerfile itself. This file decides what leaves your
# machine at all — so the Dockerfile and everything under `docker/` must stay,
# or Cloud Build has nothing to build from.
#
# Its existence also changes gcloud's behaviour: with no `.gcloudignore` it
# infers one from `.gitignore`, which happens to exclude `.env` today. Spelling
# it out means a future edit to `.gitignore` can't quietly start uploading
# secrets.
# =============================================================================

# Never leaves the machine. `.env` holds the API target for this laptop, and
# Vite bakes any VITE_* value it finds into the bundle at build time.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Reinstalled from the lockfile inside the image; uploading it is hundreds of
# megabytes and host-platform binaries that would be wrong there anyway.
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr

.git
.gitignore

# Local noise.
*.local
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# Handover notes and API references — not part of the app.
API-DOCUMENTATION*.md
LIVE-VIEW-FRONTEND-GUIDE.md
SESSION-HANDOVER.md

# Deliberately NOT ignored, because Cloud Build needs them:
#   Dockerfile
#   .dockerignore
#   docker/
#   package.json, package-lock.json
#   src/, public/, index.html, vite.config.ts, tsconfig*.json
